  "signature_visual": {
    "slide_number": 3,
    "concept": "The Reversibility Clock \u2014 a horizontal per-module timeline showing that the design deadline is release-for-fabrication, not the pour. Left band: the six modules set in August 2025 (largest 278 ft \u00d7 136 ft, 3,320 tons, placed to ~3/4-inch tolerance), drawn with their decision windows already closed months earlier in the factory. Right band: future modules with open decision windows, each window closing at 'release-for-fabrication' \u2014 annotated 'unpublished; obtain from JV (Decision D0/D2)'. A single callout carries the inversion: post-release, modular is MORE change-hostile than stick-built, because template changes propagate across the fabrication line; the ~30% cost and ~30% schedule savings DFW attributes to the method is a repetition dividend, DFW-supplied and not independently audited.",
